@meeting crossingBackSignal
// SW6 (ending writer A), the crossing back: straight after crossingBackOath, the bow lounge, the Veyli ship alongside
// (V-5's sky ship, Saturday 10:00 to Sunday 15:00). Saruth (they/them; no contractions) reads Taavek's ship's last
// signal. Taavek is they/them. No choice: a staged moment, then the address.
title: The last signal
from: Envoy Saruth
gist: Saruth read the Veyli ship's last signal to the Wren as it turned away at the Line.
== lines
saruth: Captain. Crew of the Wren. The small ship sends a signal. It asks that it be read aloud.   [gesture]
saruth: I will read it as it is written. Taavek writes the way they speak. Forgive them.
saruth: "Wren. Thank you for the round one. It spins. Very. We are at the Line. We turn here."   [listen]
saruth: "Your sky is the other way. We hope it is kind. If it is not, tell us. We come."
saruth: "Also the coffee. Very bitter. Very good. Send more." That is the end of the signal.
holt: Hm. Good neighbours, those.   [nod]
saruth > holt: Yes, Chief. They are. So are you.
marrow: Thank you, Envoy. Tell them the Wren says the same. And yes, we'll send coffee.   [laugh]
